meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: American Community Survey
    title_snapshot: American Community Survey - Place of birth of the foreign-born population
    description: |-
      The American Community Survey (ACS) is an annual survey run by the US Census Bureau. It samples about 3.5 million housing unit addresses each year and measures the demographic, social, economic, and housing characteristics of the US population. Since 2005, it has replaced the long-form questionnaire of the decennial census.
    description_snapshot: |-
      This file contains the foreign-born population of the United States by country of birth, for each year from 2005, from the ACS 1-year estimates (table B05006, "Place of Birth for the Foreign-Born Population in the United States"), retrieved through the Census Bureau data API. Each row holds one of the table's variables for one year, with the API's own variable code and label. There is no value for 2020: the Census Bureau did not release standard 1-year estimates for that year because of data-collection problems during the COVID-19 pandemic.
    date_published: "2025-09-11"

    # Citation
    producer: US Census Bureau
    citation_full: |-
      U.S. Census Bureau, American Community Survey 1-Year Estimates, Table B05006 (Place of Birth for the Foreign-Born Population in the United States).

    # Files
    url_main: https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs
    url_download: https://api.census.gov/data/2024/acs/acs1
    date_accessed: "2026-07-22"

    # License
    license:
      name: Public domain
